## Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
  User((User + Controller))
  React["React Frontend<br/>(Vite + TypeScript)"]
  Tauri["Tauri 2 Shell<br/>(Rust)"]
  SQLite[(SQLite)]
  FS["Filesystem / Processes"]
  Importers["Importers<br/>(Steam, Astris, Native)"]

  User --> React
  React -->|"invoke()"| Tauri
  Tauri --> SQLite
  Tauri --> FS
  Tauri --> Importers
  Importers --> FS
```

Windows Steam Play is a core connection layer, not a side feature. SQLite is the catalog. A saved `loginusers.vdf` in `steam-windows` is the seed for each per-game container.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  ui[Orbit UI]
  sqlite[(SQLite account + catalog)]
  seed["steam-windows prefix\nsaved login"]
  container[Per-game Wine container]
  game[Game executable]
  ui -->|"Play when signed in"| container
  sqlite --> ui
  seed --> container
  container --> game
```

Ready vs Play: the UI enables Play when `signedIn` and the title is installed. Rust clones that game's container, seeds the saved login, signs the container's Steam client on, and starts the EXE with `SteamAppId`. An expired session asks for Settings → Steam. Sign out is the only wipe.

